	(text "D3 + Q1: with USB present VSYS comes through D3 and Q1 is off; without it Q1 turns on\nand the cell feeds VSYS. The charger never carries the load.\nU3 RT9080 (L18): 600 mA, 2 uA quiescent. VBAT_SENSE = VBAT / 2 (1M/1M, ~2 uA).\nQ2: nRAIL_EN (GPIO15) LOW = +3V3_SW on. R10 holds the rail off through reset and boot."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 373.38 110.49 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0efbd9f8-baf8-5d32-a0a6-dd794e66f4b9")
	)
	(text "J2 (main) and J3 share one layout, pins 1-10 (D4, D5); J2, J12, J3 and J13 all fitted (J2: S1/S2, J3: GPIO4/GPIO5):\n  1 GND  2 SDA/A  3 SCL/B  4 3V3_SW  5 GND  6 S1/GPIO4  7 3V3_SW  8 GND  9 S2/GPIO5  10 3V3_SW\nEach is two XY308-2.54-5P blocks side by side (no 10-way part at JLCPCB): J2+J12, J3+J13.\nJP2/JP3: J3 pins 2-3 = RS485 A/B as delivered; cut 1-2 and bridge 2-3 for UART0 RX/TX (U5 must then be left off) (D29).\nJ5: holes only, no connector (L10): spare GPIO 7, 38-42, 47, 48 with GND and 3V3_SW. R16 (SENS1 pull-up) and C12 (SENS2 filter) fitted; R17, C11 not fitted.\nFirmware: switch +3V3_SW on (GPIO15 low) before any I2C or sensor access."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 271.78 248.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "15f84331-c3bd-5707-b529-de1487aaaca2")
	)
	(text "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1U MODULE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 79.7583 149.735 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1afe85cd-5ec1-5728-b6ff-e7e25d5a7637")
	)
	(text "SYSTEM POWER: LOAD SHARING, 3.3 V LDO, SWITCHED SENSOR RAIL"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 368.3 16.385 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2847906b-7ce6-5f25-8a09-ae59e054b759")
	)
	(text "Fitted by default: J3 pin 2 = A, pin 3 = B via JP2/JP3 (D29). A board without Modbus can leave out\nU5, C13, R18-R21, D5 and J3 (see COST-ESTIMATE.txt). GPIO16 = DE/RE (high = transmit, R18 = receive).\nJP4 bridged = 120R termination. RS485 sensors need their own 5-24 V supply (external)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 87.63 369.57 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4181bd36-2f4e-5217-99e1-1773264c972a")
	)
	(text "Ra-01SH (L2): SX1262 with crystal, 803-930 MHz, IPEX socket for the antenna (pad 1 ANT unused).\nThe module drives its own RF switch from DIO2 (TXEN = DIO2 inside; RXEN not connected), so\nTXEN, RXEN, DIO2 and DIO3 are left open. Own always-on regulator U7 (+3V3_RF, L18): isolates the\nradio from WiFi load steps; LoRaMesher sleeps it over SPI, never by power. C14/C15 at pin 3, C16 at U7.\nR22 keeps the radio deselected and R23 keeps it out of reset while the ESP32 boots or sleeps.\nFirmware: LoRaMesher/RadioLib defaults fit (DC-DC regulator, no TCXO, DIO2 as RF switch) (L6)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 269.24 364.49 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "755c5940-a36c-5670-8d3a-aa1c46bb1fea")
	)
	(text "USB-C sink, 5 V only: CC1/CC2 5.1k to GND. D+/D- go straight to the S3's native USB\n(GPIO20/GPIO19): no USB-UART chip and no ESD chip (D9).\nJ6: XY308-2P screw terminal for external 5 V, e.g. a solar panel (D10; fitted from D34)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 90.17 102.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7ca46c7a-cfc6-5ded-be1c-f22a1de31e40")
	)
	(text "GPIO map (L3): sensors 1/2 (ADC1) -> J2, spares 4/5 (ADC1) -> J13, VBAT_SENSE 6, I2C 17/18,\nLoRa NSS/SCK/MOSI/MISO 8-11, RST 12, BUSY 13, DIO1 14 (as Heltec V3/V4), nRAIL_EN 15,\nRS485 DE 16, UART0 43/44 -> RS485 or J3, USB 19/20, LED 21, BOOT 0.\nSpares 7, 38-42, 47, 48 -> J5 holes (L10). Not connected: straps 3, 45, 46 (internal defaults)\nand 35-37. J7 (not fitted): off-board LED, pin 1 = anode, pin 2 = cathode, shares R13.\nC8/C9 close to module pin 2. U.FL antenna: module end at the board edge, away from the LoRa antenna (L5)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.52 255.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "80347834-15bf-5763-8d74-c58ab4942d58")
	)
	(text "USB-C: 5 V IN AND PROGRAMMING"
